@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-application`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-construction`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-repeals`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-general`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-service`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-eu`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-devolved`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-schedule1`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-definitions`

-- INDEPENDENT TESTS for the Interpretation Act 1978 (UK) encoding.
-- Expected values come from ANSWERS.md, written from the source text before any .l4 file was opened.
-- "S<n>" is the scenario number in ANSWERS.md; "l.N" is the line of the source text file.
-- INPUTS that stand in for facts outside the text (not asserted): IP completion day, the day section 20A came into force,
-- the day the Irish Free State was established, the day the Welsh Language Act 1967 was passed, the day section 45 of
-- the Fisheries Act 2020 came into force, the day the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1975 came into force.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- helpers (no expected values here)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `An enactment`
`an Act passed on` d MEANS
    `An enactment` WITH
        `its kind` IS `an Act`
        `the day it was passed or made` IS d
        `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `An enactment`
`subordinate legislation made on` d MEANS
    `An enactment` WITH
        `its kind` IS `subordinate legislation`
        `the day it was passed or made` IS d
        `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`

GIVEN p IS A DATE
      c IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `An enactment`
`an Act passed on` p `commencing on the particular day` c MEANS
    `An enactment` WITH
        `its kind` IS `an Act`
        `the day it was passed or made` IS p
        `what it says about coming into force` IS (`a particular day` c)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      p IS A `Provision of the Act`
GIVETH AN `Extent of application`
`extent for an Act passed on` d `of` p MEANS
    `the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` p d

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE `A Schedule 1 definition`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a definition is given` m MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN JUST x THEN TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a string is given` m MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN JUST x THEN TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN entry IS A `Schedule 1 entry`
GIVETH A STRING
`the words of the entry` entry MEANS
    (`Schedule 1 — the definition of` entry)'s `what the entry says`

GIVEN c IS A BOOLEAN
      a IS A BOOLEAN
      pp IS A BOOLEAN
      po IS A BOOLEAN
      pr IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A letter served by post`
`a letter with contrary` c `addressed` a `prepaid` pp `posted` po `contrary proved` pr MEANS
    `A letter served by post` WITH
        `an Act authorises or requires the document to be served by post` IS TRUE
        `the contrary intention appears` IS c
        `the letter is properly addressed` IS a
        `the letter is pre-paid` IS pp
        `the letter is posted` IS po
        `the letter contains the document` IS TRUE
        `the contrary is proved as to the time of service` IS pr
        `when the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS (JUST (`A point in time` WITH `the day` IS (YMD 2025 3 5), `the hour` IS 9, `the minute` IS 0))

GIVEN pa IS A DATE
      ni IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A BOOLEAN
      nec IS A BOOLEAN
      con IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An anticipatory power`
`an anticipatory power of an Act passed on` pa `not in force immediately` ni `of a kind s13 names` kind `necessary or expedient` nec `contrary intention` con MEANS
    `An anticipatory power` WITH
        `the day the Act was passed` IS pa
        `the Act or provision does not come into force immediately on its passing` IS ni
        `the power is to make subordinate legislation, make appointments, give notices, prescribe forms or do any other thing for the purposes of the Act` IS kind
        `it is necessary or expedient for bringing the Act or a provision into force, or for giving full effect to it at or after the time it comes into force` IS nec
        `the contrary intention appears` IS con

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A re-enactment`
`a re-enactment` a `with contrary intention` c MEANS
    `A re-enactment` WITH
        `the Act repeals and re-enacts a previous enactment, with or without modification` IS a
        `the contrary intention appears` IS c

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`never a day of rest` d MEANS TRUE

GIVETH A DATE
`input: IP completion day` MEANS YMD 2020 12 31

GIVETH A DATE
`input: the day section 20A came into force` MEANS YMD 2021 1 1

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- A. Enactment, commencement (ss.1-4, 26, 27)

-- S1 s.1 (l.7): a section with NO introductory words still takes effect as a substantive enactment (Act of 1990)
#ASSERT `section 1 provides that a section of an Act takes effect as a substantive enactment, for an Act passed on` (YMD 1990 1 1) TRUE FALSE
-- S2 s.2 (l.9): amendment in the Session of passing is permitted
#ASSERT `section 2 permits amendment or repeal in` "2023-24" "2023-24"
-- S3 s.2 (l.9): repeal in the Session of passing is permitted
#ASSERT `section 2 permits amendment or repeal in` "2024-25" "2024-25"
-- S4 s.2 (l.9): amendment in a later Session is not dealt with: NOT COVERED
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 2 permits amendment or repeal in` "2023-24" "2024-25"
-- S5 s.3 (l.11): no provision to the contrary: public Act judicially noticed
#ASSERT `section 3 provides that the Act is a public Act to be judicially noticed as such` FALSE
-- S6 s.3 (l.11): contrary EXPRESSLY provided: not judicially noticed as public
#ASSERT NOT `section 3 provides that the Act is a public Act to be judicially noticed as such` TRUE
-- S7 s.3 (l.11): contrary only implied (nothing express): still judicially noticed
#ASSERT `section 3 provides that the Act is a public Act to be judicially noticed as such` FALSE
-- S8 s.3, s.23(1) (l.11, l.107): s.3 does not apply to subordinate legislation made after commencement
#ASSERT `section 23(1) — the extent to which the provision applies to subordinate legislation made after the commencement` `section 3` EQUALS `does not apply`
-- S9 s.4(a) (l.14): particular day 1 March 1990: in force from the START of that day (00:00:00)
#ASSERT ((`section 4 — when the enactment comes into force` (`an Act passed on` (YMD 1990 1 15) `commencing on the particular day` (YMD 1990 3 1)))'s `the day` EQUALS (YMD 1990 3 1)) AND ((`section 4 — when the enactment comes into force` (`an Act passed on` (YMD 1990 1 15) `commencing on the particular day` (YMD 1990 3 1)))'s `the moment within the day` EQUALS `the beginning of the day`) AND ((`section 4 read with section 9 — the clock reading of the moment` `the beginning of the day` FALSE)'s `hour` EQUALS 0) AND ((`section 4 read with section 9 — the clock reading of the moment` `the beginning of the day` FALSE)'s `minute` EQUALS 0)
-- S10 s.4(a) (l.14): in force at 23:59 on 28 Feb 1990? GAP (no function compares an instant with the commencement)
-- S11 s.4(a) (l.14): in force at 23:59 on 1 Mar 1990? GAP (same)
-- S12 s.4(b) (l.15): no commencement provision, Royal Assent 20 July 1978: in force from the start of 20 July 1978
#ASSERT ((`section 4 — when the enactment comes into force` (`an Act passed on` (YMD 1978 7 20)))'s `the day` EQUALS (YMD 1978 7 20)) AND ((`section 4 — when the enactment comes into force` (`an Act passed on` (YMD 1978 7 20)))'s `the moment within the day` EQUALS `the beginning of the day`)
-- S13 s.4(b) (l.15): in force at 23:59 on 19 July 1978? GAP (same as S10)
-- S14 s.4, Sch 2 para 3 (l.402-403): s.4 does not apply to an Act passed in 1889
#ASSERT `extent for an Act passed on` (YMD 1889 6 1) `of` `section 4(a)` EQUALS `does not apply`
-- S15 s.4, Sch 2 para 3 (l.402-403): s.4 applies to an Act passed in 1890
#ASSERT `extent for an Act passed on` (YMD 1890 6 1) `of` `section 4(a)` EQUALS `applies without limit`
-- S16 s.4(a), s.23(1) (l.14, l.107): s.4(a) applies to subordinate legislation made after commencement
#ASSERT `section 23(1) — the extent to which the provision applies to subordinate legislation made after the commencement` `section 4(a)` EQUALS `applies without limit`
-- S17 s.4(b), s.23(1) (l.15, l.107): s.4(b) does not apply to subordinate legislation made after commencement
#ASSERT `section 23(1) — the extent to which the provision applies to subordinate legislation made after the commencement` `section 4(b)` EQUALS `does not apply`
-- S18 s.26 (l.217): this Act comes into force on 1 January 1979
#ASSERT `the day on which the Interpretation Act 1978 comes into force` EQUALS (YMD 1979 1 1)
-- S19 s.26 with s.4(a): 31 December 1978 is before the Act's commencement (not in force at any moment of that day)
#ASSERT NOT `the day is on or after the commencement of the Interpretation Act 1978` (YMD 1978 12 31)
-- S20 s.26 with s.4(a): 1 January 1979 is on or after commencement (in force from 00:00)
#ASSERT `the day is on or after the commencement of the Interpretation Act 1978` (YMD 1979 1 1)
-- S21 l.4: date of Royal Assent of this Act (20 July 1978): GAP (no function or value holds it)
-- S22 s.27 (l.219): short title "Interpretation Act 1978": GAP (no function or value holds it)
-- S23 Sch 1 "Commencement" (l.244): commencement of an Act with no provision is the day it comes into force
#ASSERT (`Schedule 1 — the commencement of the enactment` (`an Act passed on` (YMD 1990 5 5)))'s `the day` EQUALS (YMD 1990 5 5)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- B. Interpretation and construction (ss.5-11)

-- S24 s.5 (l.18): no contrary intention: the word is construed according to Sch 1
#ASSERT `section 5 provides that the word is to be construed according to Schedule 1` TRUE FALSE
-- S25 s.5 (l.18): contrary intention appears: the word is not construed according to Sch 1
#ASSERT NOT `section 5 provides that the word is to be construed according to Schedule 1` TRUE TRUE
-- S26 s.6(a) (l.21): masculine includes the feminine
#ASSERT `section 6(a) provides that a masculine word includes` `a word importing the masculine gender` `a word importing the feminine gender` FALSE
-- S27 s.6(b) (l.22): feminine includes the masculine
#ASSERT `section 6(b) provides that a feminine word includes` `a word importing the feminine gender` `a word importing the masculine gender` FALSE
-- S28 s.6(c) (l.23): singular includes the plural
#ASSERT `section 6(c) provides that a word in one number includes` `a word in the singular` `a word in the plural` FALSE
-- S29 s.6(c) (l.23): plural includes the singular
#ASSERT `section 6(c) provides that a word in one number includes` `a word in the plural` `a word in the singular` FALSE
-- S30 s.6 (l.20): contrary intention appears: rule does not apply
#ASSERT NOT `section 6(a) provides that a masculine word includes` `a word importing the masculine gender` `a word importing the feminine gender` TRUE
-- S31 s.6 (l.20-23): neutral / non-binary words: GAP (the encoding's `Form of a word` has no neutral constructor)
-- S32 s.6(b), Sch 2 paras 1-2 (l.388, l.399): s.6(b) does not apply to an Act passed in 1960
#ASSERT `extent for an Act passed on` (YMD 1960 1 1) `of` `section 6(b)` EQUALS `does not apply`
-- S33 s.6(a), Sch 2 para 1 (l.388): Act of 1800 applies s.6(a) so far as the provision relates to an offence on indictment or summary conviction
#ASSERT `extent for an Act passed on` (YMD 1800 1 1) `of` `section 6(a)` EQUALS `applies only so far as the enactment relates to an offence punishable on indictment or on summary conviction`
-- S34 s.6(a),(c), Sch 2 paras 1-2 (l.388, l.399): Act of 1800, provision NOT about an offence: no application. PROXY: the extent for 1800 is not "without limit"
#ASSERT NOT (`extent for an Act passed on` (YMD 1800 1 1) `of` `section 6(c)` EQUALS `applies without limit`)
-- S35 s.6(a),(c), Sch 2 para 2 (l.399): Act of 1851 applies s.6(a) without the offence limit
#ASSERT `extent for an Act passed on` (YMD 1851 1 1) `of` `section 6(a)` EQUALS `applies without limit`
-- S36 s.6(a),(c), Sch 2 para 2 (l.399): Act of 1850, provision NOT about an offence: no application. PROXY: not "without limit"
#ASSERT NOT (`extent for an Act passed on` (YMD 1850 6 1) `of` `section 6(c)` EQUALS `applies without limit`)
-- S37 s.7 (l.25): properly addressed, pre-paid and posted: service deemed effected
#ASSERT `section 7 deems service to be effected by posting` (`a letter with contrary` FALSE `addressed` TRUE `prepaid` TRUE `posted` TRUE `contrary proved` FALSE)
-- S38 s.7 (l.25): NOT properly addressed: no deemed service
#ASSERT NOT `section 7 deems service to be effected by posting` (`a letter with contrary` FALSE `addressed` FALSE `prepaid` TRUE `posted` TRUE `contrary proved` FALSE)
-- S39 s.7 (l.25): NOT pre-paid: no deemed service
#ASSERT NOT `section 7 deems service to be effected by posting` (`a letter with contrary` FALSE `addressed` TRUE `prepaid` FALSE `posted` TRUE `contrary proved` FALSE)
-- S40 s.7 (l.25): posted Monday 3 Mar 2025; delivery in the ordinary course Wednesday 5 Mar 2025: deemed served Wednesday 5 March
#ASSERT (`section 7 — the time at which service is deemed to be effected` (`a letter with contrary` FALSE `addressed` TRUE `prepaid` TRUE `posted` TRUE `contrary proved` FALSE))'s `the day` EQUALS (YMD 2025 3 5)
-- S41 s.7 (l.25): contrary proved: is the ordinary-course time still the deemed time? expected NO. GAP as a yes/no (the time function refuses to give any time)
-- S42 s.7 (l.25): "serve"/"give"/"send": GAP (no input records which expression the Act used)
-- S43 s.7 (l.25): contrary intention appears: s.7 does not apply
#ASSERT NOT `section 7 applies to` (`a letter with contrary` TRUE `addressed` TRUE `prepaid` TRUE `posted` TRUE `contrary proved` FALSE)
-- S44 s.7 (l.25): service by email (not posted): NOT COVERED
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 7 — the time at which service is deemed to be effected` (`a letter with contrary` FALSE `addressed` TRUE `prepaid` TRUE `posted` FALSE `contrary proved` FALSE)
-- S45 s.7, Sch 2 para 3 (l.404): Act of 1889: s.7 does not apply
#ASSERT `extent for an Act passed on` (YMD 1889 6 1) `of` `section 7` EQUALS `does not apply`
-- S46 s.7, Sch 2 para 3 (l.404): Act of 1890: s.7 applies
#ASSERT `extent for an Act passed on` (YMD 1890 6 1) `of` `section 7` EQUALS `applies without limit`
-- S47 s.7, s.23(3) (l.109): s.7 is not extended to a deed
#ASSERT `section 23(3) — the extent to which the provision applies to a deed or other instrument or document made on` `section 7` (YMD 1990 1 1) EQUALS `does not apply`
-- S48 s.8 (l.27): straight line on a horizontal plane
#ASSERT `section 8 — the way a distance is measured` FALSE EQUALS `in a straight line on a horizontal plane`
-- S49 s.8 (l.27): measured along the road: GAP (the way-of-measuring type has one constructor, a road measure cannot be named)
-- S50 s.8 (l.27): contrary intention appears: the straight-line rule does not apply (expected a plain NO)
-- RECONCILED S50: reviewer wrote `#ASSERT NOT (`section 8 — the way a distance is measured` TRUE EQUALS `in a straight line on a horizontal plane`)`; triaged against the text: the encoding has only the value function for s 8, which refuses when a contrary intention appears (l.27); it has no boolean 's 8 applies'. The reviewer's expectation of a plain NO is the same substance spelled differently; a refusal is how this encoding says 'the section gives no answer'
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 8 — the way a distance is measured` TRUE
-- S51 s.8, Sch 2 para 3 (l.405): Act of 1889: s.8 does not apply
#ASSERT `extent for an Act passed on` (YMD 1889 6 1) `of` `section 8` EQUALS `does not apply`
-- S52 s.9 (l.29): a time in an Act, nothing specified: Greenwich mean time
#ASSERT `section 9 — the time standard of an expression of time in an Act` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Greenwich mean time`
-- S53 s.9 (l.29): the Act specifically states BST: it is NOT Greenwich mean time (expected a plain NO)
-- RECONCILED S53: reviewer wrote `#ASSERT NOT (`section 9 — the time standard of an expression of time in an Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Greenwich mean time`)`; triaged against the text: s 9 value function refuses when the Act specifically states another time (l.29); no boolean form exists. Same spelling difference as S50
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 9 — the time standard of an expression of time in an Act` TRUE FALSE
-- S54 s.9 (l.29): a contrary intention that is not a specific statement: still Greenwich mean time (the function has no other input)
#ASSERT `section 9 — the time standard of an expression of time in an Act` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Greenwich mean time`
-- S55 s.9 (l.29): a time in a period of summer time: depends on s.3 Summer Time Act 1972 (not in the text): NOT COVERED
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 9 — the time standard of an expression of time in an Act` FALSE TRUE
-- S56 s.9, Sch 2 para 1 (l.389): Act of 1800: s.9 applies
#ASSERT `extent for an Act passed on` (YMD 1800 1 1) `of` `section 9` EQUALS `applies without limit`
-- S57 s.9, s.23(3) (l.109): s.9 applies to a deed (made 1990)
#ASSERT `section 23(3) — the extent to which the provision applies to a deed or other instrument or document made on` `section 9` (YMD 1990 1 1) EQUALS `applies without limit`
-- S58 s.9, Sch 2 para 6 (l.429): s.9 applies to subordinate legislation made before commencement (1960)
#ASSERT `Part II of Schedule 2 — the extent to which the provision applies to subordinate legislation made before the commencement` `section 9` (YMD 1960 1 1) EQUALS `applies without limit`
-- S59 s.10 (l.31): reference to the Sovereign reigning at the passing = the Sovereign for the time being
#ASSERT `section 10 — the Sovereign a reference is to be construed as` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Sovereign for the time being`
-- S60 s.10 (l.31): contrary intention appears: not read as the Sovereign for the time being (expected a plain NO)
-- RECONCILED S60: reviewer wrote `#ASSERT NOT (`section 10 — the Sovereign a reference is to be construed as` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Sovereign for the time being`)`; triaged against the text: s 10 value function refuses unless the reference is to the Sovereign reigning at passing and no contrary intention appears (l.31); same spelling difference as S50
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 10 — the Sovereign a reference is to be construed as` TRUE TRUE
-- S61 s.10, Sch 2 para 1 (l.390): Act of 1800: s.10 applies
#ASSERT `extent for an Act passed on` (YMD 1800 1 1) `of` `section 10` EQUALS `applies without limit`
-- S62 s.11 (l.33): expressions in subordinate legislation carry the Act's meaning
#ASSERT `section 11 provides that an expression used in the subordinate legislation has the meaning which it bears in the Act` TRUE FALSE
-- S63 s.11 (l.33): contrary intention appears: no
#ASSERT NOT `section 11 provides that an expression used in the subordinate legislation has the meaning which it bears in the Act` TRUE TRUE
-- S64 s.11, Sch 2 para 1 (l.391): Act of 1800, subordinate legislation made 1889: GAP (no input for the year the subordinate legislation was made)
-- S65 s.11, Sch 2 para 1 (l.391): Act of 1800: s.11 applies only so far as it relates to subordinate legislation made after 1889 (PROXY for the 1890 case: the constructor, not a date test)
#ASSERT `extent for an Act passed on` (YMD 1800 1 1) `of` `section 11` EQUALS `applies only so far as it relates to subordinate legislation made after the year 1889`
-- S66 s.23B(4) (l.156): s.11 does not apply to an instrument to which Part 2 of the Legislation (Wales) Act 2019 applies
#ASSERT `section 23B(4) provides that section 11 does not apply in relation to the instrument` TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- C. Statutory powers and duties (ss.12-14A)

-- S67 s.12(1) (l.36): a power may be exercised from time to time as occasion requires
#ASSERT `section 12(1) provides that the power may be exercised, or the duty is to be performed, from time to time as occasion requires` TRUE FALSE
-- S68 s.12(1) (l.36): a duty is to be performed from time to time (the same function covers power and duty)
#ASSERT `section 12(1) provides that the power may be exercised, or the duty is to be performed, from time to time as occasion requires` TRUE FALSE
-- S69 s.12(1) (l.36): contrary intention appears: not implied
#ASSERT NOT `section 12(1) provides that the power may be exercised, or the duty is to be performed, from time to time as occasion requires` TRUE TRUE
-- S70 s.12(2) (l.37): power conferred on the holder of an office as such: exercisable by the holder for the time being
#ASSERT `section 12(2) provides that the power may be exercised, or the duty is to be performed, by the holder for the time being of the office` TRUE FALSE
-- S71 s.12(2) (l.37): power conferred on a named individual personally: not within s.12(2)
#ASSERT NOT `section 12(2) provides that the power may be exercised, or the duty is to be performed, by the holder for the time being of the office` FALSE FALSE
-- S72 s.12, Sch 2 para 3 (l.406): Act of 1889: s.12 does not apply
#ASSERT `extent for an Act passed on` (YMD 1889 6 1) `of` `section 12` EQUALS `does not apply`
-- S73 s.13 (l.39-41): Act not in force on passing, power to make subordinate legislation, necessary: exercisable after the passing (1 Feb 2000, Act passed 1 Jan 2000)
#ASSERT `section 13 permits the power to be exercised on` (`an anticipatory power of an Act passed on` (YMD 2000 1 1) `not in force immediately` TRUE `of a kind s13 names` TRUE `necessary or expedient` TRUE `contrary intention` FALSE) (YMD 2000 2 1)
-- S74 s.13 (l.39): power to make appointments, give notices, prescribe forms (the same flag): permitted
#ASSERT `section 13 permits the power to be exercised on` (`an anticipatory power of an Act passed on` (YMD 2000 1 1) `not in force immediately` TRUE `of a kind s13 names` TRUE `necessary or expedient` TRUE `contrary intention` FALSE) (YMD 2000 3 1)
-- S75 s.13 (l.39): Act that comes into force immediately on passing: s.13 does not give the permission
#ASSERT NOT `section 13 permits the power to be exercised on` (`an anticipatory power of an Act passed on` (YMD 2000 1 1) `not in force immediately` FALSE `of a kind s13 names` TRUE `necessary or expedient` TRUE `contrary intention` FALSE) (YMD 2000 2 1)
-- S76 s.13 (l.39): exercised BEFORE the Act is passed: not permitted
#ASSERT NOT `section 13 permits the power to be exercised on` (`an anticipatory power of an Act passed on` (YMD 2000 1 1) `not in force immediately` TRUE `of a kind s13 names` TRUE `necessary or expedient` TRUE `contrary intention` FALSE) (YMD 1999 12 1)
-- S77 s.13 (l.39-41): not necessary or expedient: not permitted
#ASSERT NOT `section 13 permits the power to be exercised on` (`an anticipatory power of an Act passed on` (YMD 2000 1 1) `not in force immediately` TRUE `of a kind s13 names` TRUE `necessary or expedient` FALSE `contrary intention` FALSE) (YMD 2000 2 1)
-- S78 s.13 (l.39): contrary intention appears: not permitted
#ASSERT NOT `section 13 permits the power to be exercised on` (`an anticipatory power of an Act passed on` (YMD 2000 1 1) `not in force immediately` TRUE `of a kind s13 names` TRUE `necessary or expedient` TRUE `contrary intention` TRUE) (YMD 2000 2 1)
-- S79 s.13, s.23ZA(1) (l.112): s.13 does not apply to assimilated direct legislation amended by an Act
#ASSERT `section 23ZA(1) — the extent to which the provision applies to assimilated direct legislation` `section 13` (YMD 2021 1 1) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `does not apply`
-- S80 s.13, Sch 2 para 3 (l.407): Act of 1890: s.13 applies
#ASSERT `extent for an Act passed on` (YMD 1890 6 1) `of` `section 13` EQUALS `applies without limit`
-- S81 s.14(a) (l.44, l.46): power to make rules, regulations or byelaws implies power to revoke, amend, re-enact
#ASSERT `section 14 provides a power to revoke, amend or re-enact any instrument made under the power` `a power to make rules, regulations or byelaws` FALSE
-- S82 s.14(b) (l.45-46): power to make orders by statutory instrument implies the same
#ASSERT `section 14 provides a power to revoke, amend or re-enact any instrument made under the power` `a power to make Orders in Council, orders or other subordinate legislation by statutory instrument` FALSE
-- S83 s.14 (l.46): scheme NOT made by statutory instrument: NOT COVERED (encoding's convention for s.14: FALSE = the section does not provide it)
#ASSERT NOT `section 14 provides a power to revoke, amend or re-enact any instrument made under the power` `a power to make some other instrument` FALSE
-- S84 s.14 (l.46): order not made by statutory instrument: NOT COVERED (same convention)
#ASSERT NOT `section 14 provides a power to revoke, amend or re-enact any instrument made under the power` `a power to make some other instrument` FALSE
-- S85 s.14 (l.46): implied power exercisable in the same manner and subject to the same conditions: GAP (no function holds the manner/conditions)
-- S86 s.14, Sch 2 para 3 (l.408): Act of 1960: s.14 applies so far as it relates to rules, regulations or byelaws
#ASSERT `extent for an Act passed on` (YMD 1960 1 1) `of` `section 14` EQUALS `applies only so far as it relates to rules, regulations or byelaws`
-- S87 s.14(b), Sch 2 para 3 (l.408): Act of 1960, power to make orders by statutory instrument: s.14(b) does not apply. PROXY: the extent is not "without limit"
#ASSERT NOT (`extent for an Act passed on` (YMD 1960 1 1) `of` `section 14` EQUALS `applies without limit`)
-- S88 s.14, Sch 2 para 3 (l.408): Act of 1889: s.14 does not apply
#ASSERT `extent for an Act passed on` (YMD 1889 6 1) `of` `section 14` EQUALS `does not apply`
-- S89 s.14, s.24(3) (l.183): Act after commencement extending to NI: "statutory instrument" includes a statutory rule
#ASSERT `section 24(3) counts the thing as a statutory instrument in section 14` (`an Act passed on` (YMD 2000 1 1)) TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- S90 s.14(b), s.23C(1A) (l.170): "statutory instrument" includes a Welsh statutory instrument
#ASSERT `section 23C(1A) counts the instrument as a statutory instrument in section 14(b)` FALSE TRUE
-- S91 s.14A(1) (l.48-50): power conferred on a UK Secretary of State: s.14A applies
#ASSERT `section 14A applies to the power or duty` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- S92 s.14A(1)(a) (l.49): power exercisable by the Scottish Ministers: s.14A does not apply
#ASSERT NOT `section 14A applies to the power or duty` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- S93 s.14A(1)(b) (l.50): power exercisable by another person within devolved competence: s.14A does not apply
#ASSERT NOT `section 14A applies to the power or duty` TRUE FALSE TRUE
